# Random modules in which some predicates are declared without a
# determinism, among them ones whose bodies call the others and each other,
# recursively or not, with committed choice calls, determinism casts and
# requirements (generate-switch-programs.py --determinism --committed
# --casts --requires --inferred). merkc must infer the determinisms of the
# procedures and their goals that mmc does, and report its errors, those
# for committed choice calls in their bodies among them, at the same
# lines.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-switch-programs.py --determinism --committed --casts --requires --inferred --seed 17 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-switches --determinism %t/*.m
